  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.6,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["U22", "U15", "U35", "U36", "R63", "D29"],
      "pins": ["U22.2", "U35.4", "U36.1", "U36.4"],
      "nets": ["GND", "ESTOP_SINK_ALL", "ESTOP_OUT"],
      "obs": "On the 'LED Enable and E-Stop Config' sheet the open-drain sink buffer U22 (SN74LVC1G07) has its input A (pin 2) tied directly to GND, while its /OE (pin 1) is the ESTOP_SINK1 control. Because a 1G07 only sinks when A is high, U22's output (pin 4) is permanently high-impedance, so U15's input (A = U22.Y) is always pulled high by R61, making U15 sink whenever enabled and pulling U35's input (A = U15.Y) low, so U35 can never sink. Consequently ESTOP_SINK_ALL (U35.Y) is held high by R63, which keeps U36's /OE high, so U36 never sinks and ESTOP_OUT never asserts. The branch-1 indicator LED D29 (on U22.Y) can therefore never light.",
      "exp": "The specification states these buffers are 'wired as /OE-controlled sinks, feeding an ESTOP_OUT signal' and confirms the e-stop circuit actually works ('e-stop should activate if a cable is disconnected. - nevermind, it does this'). For the sink chain to assert ESTOP_OUT (and for the per-branch indicator lights added in the July 2024 changelog), U22's input A must be tied high (e.g. to +3V3), not to GND.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "U22 pin 2 wire terminates at a GND symbol; U22 pin 1 (/OE) = ESTOP_SINK1 via R32; U35 pin 4 = ESTOP_SINK_ALL with R63 10k to +3V3 (sheet 'LED Enable and E-Stop Config')"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "U36 pin 1 (/OE) = ESTOP_SINK_ALL via R57, pin 4 = ESTOP_OUT (sheet 'Motion Sensing' / CAN area)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "e-stop should activate if a cable is disconnected. - nevermind, it does this"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "U15, U22, U35, U36 (SN74LVC1G07) ... wired as /OE-controlled sinks, feeding an ESTOP_OUT signal shared with the CAN connectors J2/J13"}
      ],
      "impact": "The safety e-stop output (ESTOP_OUT) to the CAN connectors J2/J13 never activates, defeating the e-stop function; the ESTOP_SINK1 branch indicator LED D29 also never lights. The board would not shut down motors on an e-stop event as intended.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic otherwise matches the spec (CM4 carrier, CAN0/CAN1 with 16 MHz crystals, LTC4412 USB path, ISL54222 mux, WS2812 chain, SM712 TVS on the CAN lines), but the e-stop sink chain is broken: U22's open-drain input is tied to GND instead of high, which cascades so that ESTOP_SINK_ALL stays high and ESTOP_OUT can never assert, contradicting the spec's statement that the e-stop circuit works."
}

